.TH SDL_HINT_JOYSTICK_HIDAPI_GIP_RESET_FOR_METADATA 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_JOYSTICK_HIDAPI_GIP_RESET_FOR_METADATA \- A variable controlling whether the new HIDAPI driver for wired Xbox One (GIP) controllers should reset the controller if it can\(aqt get the metadata from the controller.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_JOYSTICK_HIDAPI_GIP_RESET_FOR_METADATA \(dqSDL_JOYSTICK_HIDAPI_GIP_RESET_FOR_METADATA\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The variable can be set to the following values:
.PP

\(bu \(dq0\(dq: Assume this is a generic controller\[char46]
.PP
\(bu \(dq1\(dq: Reset the controller to get metadata\[char46]
.PP
By default the controller is reset\[char46] This is so we can properly detect the controller type\[char46]
.PP
This hint should be set before initializing joysticks and gamepads\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]4\[char46]0\[char46]

